{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "OmniSec Unified Product Security Platform",
          "version": "1.0.0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/OWASP",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CWE-287",
              "name": "[Spoofing] Adversary JWT Forgery or Replay via Weak Signature / ",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "[Spoofing] Adversary JWT Forgery or Replay via Weak Signature / Missing Alg Enforcement (Ingress / Reverse Proxy)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Adversary signs forged authentication tokens using HMAC secret or 'none' algorithm to spoof arbitrary administrative identities.\nBusiness Impact: Full authentication bypass across all backend microservices."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://owasp.org/www-project-threat-dragon/",
              "help": {
                "text": "Remediation: Security Architecture Mitigation: Enforce strict RS256/ES256 asymmetric signature validation with centralized JWKS and reject tokens missing non-reusable 'jti' claim.",
                "markdown": "### Remediation Guidance\nSecurity Architecture Mitigation: Enforce strict RS256/ES256 asymmetric signature validation with centralized JWKS and reject tokens missing non-reusable 'jti' claim.\n\n*References:*\n- https://owasp.org/www-project-threat-dragon/\n- https://owasp.org/www-community/Threat_Modeling_Process\n- https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1078/"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stage-1",
                  "owasp threat dragon (stride/linddun)"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CWE-89",
              "name": "[Tampering] SQL Injection & Transaction State Alteration via Uns",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "[Tampering] SQL Injection & Transaction State Alteration via Unsanitized Parameters (Primary Database Store)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Untrusted parameters in database query building allow attackers to alter database record state and bypass logic barriers.\nBusiness Impact: Arbitrary record extraction, corruption of financial balances, or DB administrative takeover."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://owasp.org/www-project-threat-dragon/",
              "help": {
                "text": "Remediation: Security Architecture Mitigation: Mandate ORM-level parameterized statements, disable dynamic raw query concatenation, and apply row-level DB access controls.",
                "markdown": "### Remediation Guidance\nSecurity Architecture Mitigation: Mandate ORM-level parameterized statements, disable dynamic raw query concatenation, and apply row-level DB access controls.\n\n*References:*\n- https://owasp.org/www-project-threat-dragon/\n- https://owasp.org/www-community/Threat_Modeling_Process\n- https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1190/"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stage-1",
                  "owasp threat dragon (stride/linddun)"
                ],
                "security-severity": "10"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CWE-778",
              "name": "[Repudiation] Missing Non-Repudiation Audit Logs on State-Alteri",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "[Repudiation] Missing Non-Repudiation Audit Logs on State-Altering Operations (Application Backend API)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Financial transfers, password resets, and permission grants lack immutable transaction audit logs.\nBusiness Impact: Inability to perform post-incident forensic attribution or prove attacker culpability."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://owasp.org/www-project-threat-dragon/",
              "help": {
                "text": "Remediation: Security Architecture Mitigation: Emit structured JSON audit events to append-only, tamper-evident log stores with actor ID, IP, and UTC timestamp.",
                "markdown": "### Remediation Guidance\nSecurity Architecture Mitigation: Emit structured JSON audit events to append-only, tamper-evident log stores with actor ID, IP, and UTC timestamp.\n\n*References:*\n- https://owasp.org/www-project-threat-dragon/\n- https://owasp.org/www-community/Threat_Modeling_Process\n- https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1565/"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stage-1",
                  "owasp threat dragon (stride/linddun)"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CWE-209",
              "name": "[Information Disclosure] Verbose Server Headers & Production Sta",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "[Information Disclosure] Verbose Server Headers & Production Stack Trace Leakage (Ingress / Reverse Proxy)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "API Gateway returns internal stack traces, container environment details, and server versions upon unhandled exceptions.\nBusiness Impact: Reveals technology topology and sensitive internal variable names to unauthenticated actors."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://owasp.org/www-project-threat-dragon/",
              "help": {
                "text": "Remediation: Security Architecture Mitigation: Implement global exception handling middleware with sanitized generic error envelopes and suppress Server/X-Powered-By banners.",
                "markdown": "### Remediation Guidance\nSecurity Architecture Mitigation: Implement global exception handling middleware with sanitized generic error envelopes and suppress Server/X-Powered-By banners.\n\n*References:*\n- https://owasp.org/www-project-threat-dragon/\n- https://owasp.org/www-community/Threat_Modeling_Process\n- https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1592/"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stage-1",
                  "owasp threat dragon (stride/linddun)"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CWE-400",
              "name": "[Denial of Service] Resource Exhaustion via Unbounded Queries & ",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "[Denial of Service] Resource Exhaustion via Unbounded Queries & Lack of Rate Limiting (API4) (Application Backend API)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Endpoints accepting pagination or cryptographic hashing lack request rate limiting and payload size bounds.\nBusiness Impact: Denial of service for legitimate users and denial-of-wallet cloud billing spikes."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://owasp.org/www-project-threat-dragon/",
              "help": {
                "text": "Remediation: Security Architecture Mitigation: Deploy token-bucket rate limiters at reverse proxy (e.g. NGINX/Envoy), enforce max body size caps, and enforce hard page limits (max 100).",
                "markdown": "### Remediation Guidance\nSecurity Architecture Mitigation: Deploy token-bucket rate limiters at reverse proxy (e.g. NGINX/Envoy), enforce max body size caps, and enforce hard page limits (max 100).\n\n*References:*\n- https://owasp.org/www-project-threat-dragon/\n- https://owasp.org/www-community/Threat_Modeling_Process\n- https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1499/"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stage-1",
                  "owasp threat dragon (stride/linddun)"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CWE-639",
              "name": "[Elevation of Privilege] Broken Object Level Authorization (BOLA",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "[Elevation of Privilege] Broken Object Level Authorization (BOLA / IDOR) on Data Resources (API1) (Application Backend API)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Endpoint controllers read resource identifiers from request paths without verifying caller tenant ownership.\nBusiness Impact: Standard users can access, alter, or delete records belonging to any other user or organization."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://owasp.org/www-project-threat-dragon/",
              "help": {
                "text": "Remediation: Security Architecture Mitigation: Enforce strict authorization checks in data layer scoping all queries to current_user.tenant_id.",
                "markdown": "### Remediation Guidance\nSecurity Architecture Mitigation: Enforce strict authorization checks in data layer scoping all queries to current_user.tenant_id.\n\n*References:*\n- https://owasp.org/www-project-threat-dragon/\n- https://owasp.org/www-community/Threat_Modeling_Process\n- https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1068/"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stage-1",
                  "owasp threat dragon (stride/linddun)"
                ],
                "security-severity": "10"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CWE-798",
              "name": "[ASVS V8.3.1] Non-compliant: Verify sensitive keys, passwords, a",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "[ASVS V8.3.1] Non-compliant: Verify sensitive keys, passwords, and tokens are never stored in sourc..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "OWASP ASVS Requirement V8.3.1 (Level 1):\nVerify sensitive keys, passwords, and tokens are never stored in source code repositories.\nEvidence: Plaintext cloud/API secrets committed in .env"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://owasp.org/www-project-application-security-verification-standard/",
              "help": {
                "text": "Remediation: Remove secrets from source files and inject via environment secrets managers.",
                "markdown": "### Remediation Guidance\nRemove secrets from source files and inject via environment secrets managers.\n\n*References:*\n- https://owasp.org/www-project-application-security-verification-standard/"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stage-2",
                  "owasp asvs v4.0.3"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CWE-256",
              "name": "Hardcoded Secret: Database URI with Plaintext Password",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Hardcoded Secret: Database URI with Plaintext Password"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Potential high-entropy secret (Database URI with Plaintext Password) discovered in .env:3."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Secrets_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html",
              "help": {
                "text": "Remediation: Extract credential into an environment variable or secrets vault (e.g. AWS Secrets Manager, HashiCorp Vault). Revoke currently exposed secret.",
                "markdown": "### Remediation Guidance\nExtract credential into an environment variable or secrets vault (e.g. AWS Secrets Manager, HashiCorp Vault). Revoke currently exposed secret.\n\n*References:*\n- https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Secrets_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stage-3",
                  "gitleaks (engine)"
                ],
                "security-severity": "10"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CWE-502",
              "name": "Unsafe YAML Deserialization (RCE Risk)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Unsafe YAML Deserialization (RCE Risk)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Called `yaml.load()` without SafeLoader in server.py:47."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://pyyaml.org/wiki/PyYAMLDocumentation",
              "help": {
                "text": "Remediation: Replace `yaml.load()` with `yaml.safe_load()`.",
                "markdown": "### Remediation Guidance\nReplace `yaml.load()` with `yaml.safe_load()`.\n\n*References:*\n- https://pyyaml.org/wiki/PyYAMLDocumentation"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stage-3",
                  "semgrep ast engine"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CWE-1395",
              "name": "Vulnerable Dependency: flask@2.2.2 (CVE-2023-30861)",
              "shortDescription": {
